# Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP — SQL Query Repository

A curated collection of consultant-grade SQL queries for **Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP 26B**, organized by module, fully parameterized (no client data) and documented with a standard header in every file.

Originally written on real implementation projects (EBS R12 era), converted and remapped to Fusion Cloud 26B tables and views, then cleaned, parameterized and documented with AI-assisted refactoring.

## Structure

| Folder | Module | Queries |
|---|---|---|
| [GL](./GL) | General Ledger | Trial balance by segment · Journal lines (razão) · SLA account analysis |
| [AP](./AP) | Payables | Open invoices aging · Invoice distributions with PO · Invoices on hold |
| [FA](./FA) | Assets | Multi-book depreciation comparison · Cost transactions by period · Categories by book |
| [CE](./CE) | Cash Management | Internal bank account setup with BU and GL accounts |

## How to use

1. Open the module folder and read its `README.md` to pick a query.
2. Every `.sql` file starts with a header describing Purpose, Tables Used, Report Output, Parameters and Notes.
3. Replace the `:p_*` bind variables with your values (BIP data models accept them natively as parameters).
4. Adjust `SEGMENTn` references to your Chart of Accounts structure — segment roles vary by implementation.

See [CONVENTIONS.md](./CONVENTIONS.md) for the parameterization standard and the full EBS → Fusion mapping used in the conversion.

## Disclaimer

Queries target Fusion Cloud 26B and were validated against Oracle's official schema documentation (Tables and Views for Financials). Always test in a non-production environment first; column availability can vary by release and your security profile (data security predicates apply in BIP).

